    """Whether a staged 201 response is backed by the committed write set.

    Used at startup settlement when the operation record persisted its
    exact success response before the commit-point append. The on-disk
    committed state must actually support that response: the named
    version(s) exist on the write-set keys, a restore's key set and policy
    flag match. Records without a staged response (older bindings, crafted
    recovery scenes) skip this and rely on the artifact checks alone.
